  "method": [
    "The same native fixtures ran against the base SQL and the changed SQL. Setup, validation reads after each measurement, reference acquisition, and accepted-baseline setup are excluded. Failed batches are checked for rollback but omitted from cost totals because D1 returns no successful per-statement metadata.",
    "The baseline run temporarily used soft assertions in the new test suite to collect all cost observations despite expected failures. False/NULL rollback and profile conflicts remained enforced. The complete task patch was restored byte-for-byte afterward.",
    "For first() reads, the measurement wrapper executes the same SQL through all() to retain native metadata. This wrapper is enabled for Submit fixtures only when VISONAUT_D1_COST_REPORT is set.",
    "Each Submit fixture has one capture. The unchanged fixture borrows an accepted baseline image and adds one new profile. The zero-pixel changed fixture uploads one original and is normalized to unchanged. The changed-with-mask fixture stores one original and one mask with one new profile.",
    "Staging covers declareStaged, uploads, finalizeStaged, and terminalGitHub. Materialization covers materializeWorkflowRun. Admission, baseline seed/promotion, provider network latency, later retention, and cleanup are excluded. Random fixture identities and accumulated fixture state can affect reads; these counts are not guaranteed production savings.",
    "The status fixture has two previously delivered rows, one eligible pending row, and one later-revision pending row. Acknowledgement-only counts isolate the UPDATE; operation totals also include current-check and status-intent work. Existing delivered timestamps remain unchanged.",
    "The SQL-only step leaves broader issue #226 metadata, migration, index and manifest-storage work open."
